# health v2.9 — WARNING. "moderate" written to clinical:criticality.
#
# WHY THIS EXACT VALUE, AND NOT A NONSENSE STRING. "moderate" is a real code and
# it is legal on this very record: health:allergySeverity binds
# AllergyIntolerance.reaction.severity to mild | moderate | severe, and
# "moderate" is the middle member of that set. It is NOT in
# AllergyIntolerance.criticality, which is low | high | unable-to-assess.
#
# So this fixture is not testing that a shape rejects gibberish. It is testing
# the one confusion the release exists to prevent: criticality and reaction
# severity are two axes with two value sets, and the value that gives them away
# is the one that is correct on the other axis. A converter that folds
# AllergyIntolerance.criticality into health:allergySeverity -- the behaviour
# health v2.9 documents against -- produces exactly this record when it runs the
# fold backwards, and nothing before this binding existed would have noticed.
#
# It is also what fails if someone later "harmonises" the two sets by admitting
# mild | moderate | severe here, which would make the two predicates
# interchangeable and the distinction unrecoverable.
#
# sh:Warning, not sh:Violation, per the core v3.5 ratchet: this is the first
# release to bind clinical:criticality on any shape and pods may already carry
# it. Nothing rejects this record, and the fixture asserts exactly that
# alongside the warning.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix health: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/health/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:a11e0209-0000-4000-8000-000000000002> a health:AllergyRecord ;
    health:allergen "Penicillin G" ;
    health:allergenCode <http://www.nlm.nih.gov/research/umls/rxnorm/7980> ;
    health:allergyCategory "medication" ;
    health:reaction "Hives" ;
    clinical:criticality "moderate" ;
    clinical:status "active" ;
    clinical:sourceEHR "Meridian Health System" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.4" .
